Fedora Remix LiveMedia — container requirements (implemented by Containerfile + entrypoint.sh)

Goal
  Podman image that runs the same flow as a physical host:
    cd ~/workspace/Setup
    python3 Prepare_Web_Files.py
    python3 Prepare_LiveMedia_Build.py
    cd /livemedia-creator/FedoraRemix
    ./LiveMedia_Enhanced_Build_Script.sh

Base image
  fedora:${FEDORA_VERSION} (build-arg from config.yml via ./build.sh)

RPMs (high level)
  lorax, pykickstart — livemedia-creator / ksflatten
  anaconda — required on PATH for livemedia-creator --no-virt (directory/image install without qemu)
  httpd, rsync, python3-pyyaml — Prepare_Web_Files.py
  sshfs — kickstarts / tooling
  systemd — PID 1 for loop devices + entrypoint service
  osbuild-selinux — load policy in entrypoint before anaconda chroot relabel
  util-linux-script — dependency parity with Prepare_LiveMedia_Build on newer Fedora

Runtime mounts (see Build_LiveMedia.sh)
  Repo → /root/workspace
  Host output dir → /livemedia-creator
  SSH key → /root/github_id (see ssh_config)

Image name
  ghcr.io/<GitHub_Registry_Owner>/fedora-livemedia-builder:<Fedora_Version>
